## Negative probes — each fired, each reverted

| Probe | Exit | Diagnostic |
|---|---|---|
| `toolchain_path` added to `buildCommandV8` | 1 | the schema-8 positive case stops validating; the wire-surface gate is defense in depth behind it here |
| `download_url` added to `skillBuildTargetV2` | 1 | the generated `invalid-target-download_url` case starts validating |
| `probe.freebsd` on the `go` entry | 1 | `complete registry entry 'go' declares a probe for ['freebsd'], which is outside its platforms set and therefore unreachable` |
| the `incompatible` reason removed from the catalog | 1 | `(go, incompatible) does not resolve for linux: no active exact entry and no active any entry` |
| fixture class 3 changed to 2 for `go 1.23rc1` | 1 | `alignment row ('go', '1.23rc1') says class 2, the probe says 3` |
| restore, re-run `validate.py` | 0 | validated 48 schemas and 593 vector files |

Honest note on the first two: `validate_schemas` runs before
`validate_toolchain_contract`, so on the CLI path those two defects are caught by
the compiled validators first. The wire-surface gate is exercised directly by
`ToolchainContractTests.test_wire_surface_rejects_a_resolution_input_property`
and by a standalone run that plants `toolchain_path`, `mirror`,
`install_command` and `trust_root` on all four definitions — each fires with the
matched fragment named.

## Files changed versus the accepted base

47 entries. New: 6 schemas, 5 vector files, 6 schema-case directories, 7
generator files, `tools/toolchain_gate.py`, `tools/toolchain-boundary-probe/`,
and the two prerequisite decision records and reference document. Modified:
`CHANGELOG.md`, `COMPATIBILITY.md`, `Makefile`, `SECURITY.md`,
`conformance/README.md`, `profiles/manager.md`, `protocol/core.md`,
`schemas/v1/README.md`, `schemas/v1/common.schema.json`,
`tools/generate-vectors/main.go`, `tools/release_gate.py`, `tools/validate.py`,
`tools/test_release_gate.py`, `tools/test_validate.py`, and the three generated
artifacts (`conformance/v1/manifest.json`, `schema-cases/index.json`,
`release/1.0.0-rc.5.json`).

One rename inside accepted predecessor code: `RESERVED_WIRE_SHAPES` became
`TOOLCHAIN_WIRE_SHAPES` in `tools/validate.py` and its tests, because the three
shapes are no longer reserved. The table's contents and every check over it are
unchanged; decision 0008's own required-terms check reads the definition names,
not the constant name, so it is unaffected. Two of that suite's tests were
updated for the same reason — the driver-bearing set is now the union of both
tables, and `_minted` reuses the shipped property schemas so a synthetic stub no
longer breaks the unrelated end-to-end rejection proof.

`sys.dont_write_bytecode = True` was added to `validate.py` and
`release_gate.py`. Importing a sibling module writes `tools/__pycache__`, which
left the checkout dirty and failed the release gate's own clean-checkout
requirement — caught by the clean probe, not by reasoning.

## Reviewer focus

1. Whether `source_ref.surface` gaining `registry` is the right completion, or
   whether the conflict payload should carry the baseline some other way — a
   separate `baseline` member, or a bound-attribution union that leaves
   `source_ref` at three tokens.
2. Whether closing `toolchainRequirementV1.id` to `{go, kotlin, rust, swift}`
   rather than to the driver's primary is right. It is what keeps
   `id_not_primary` and `unknown_id` reachable as runtime violations instead of
   collapsing them into a schema rejection, and inventory case 21 depends on it —
   but it does mean a schema-8 manifest can name `rust` and be structurally
   valid.
3. Whether the `rust` `channel` classifier's `prerelease-track` class should
   yield `unclassifiable`, which is the only closed assertion token available for
   a value that is classifiable but whose assertion is not a canonical
   requirement, or whether the token set needs a third member.
4. Whether attaching `expected_metadata_sources` to a reserved registry entry is
   the right home for the disposition table cases 15–16 and 55–60 exercise, or
   whether those cases should live outside the registry document entirely until
   `TASK-260728-12pnm1` completes the entry.
5. That the candidate deliberately still says `1.0.0-rc.5` while shipping schema
   8, leaving the rc.6 mint to `TASK-260728-251p01`.
